{"reference":"Judges 16","book":"Judges","chapter":16,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Samson’s Limited Deliverance","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Samson’s final act is not presented as the complete liberation of Israel from the Philistines. Earlier in his story, he was announced as one who would begin that deliverance, and the narrative never says that he finished it. This frames Judges 16 as the end of Samson’s own story while leaving the larger conflict unresolved.","verse_refs":["Judges 13:1-25","Judges 14:1-20","Judges 15:1-20"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_judges_016_79869b195c5261447fd75474"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}